# SRG-APP-000780-AU-000190  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement an audit reduction capability that
# does not alter original content or time ordering of audit records.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000780-AU-000190
group:           V-263565
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003828
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Splunk reduces audit records at search time over the stored rawdata
                 journal, so reduction does not of itself rewrite the stored record. The
                 product does expose settings that write to the stored event or that
                 remove, hash or replace field values, so the application's share is that
                 none of them is applied to audit data, and that rawdata hashing is enabled
                 so the stored content can be shown unaltered.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.
governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.
governs:         transforms.conf - Rules that rewrite or route data as it is processed.

check:           transforms.conf [<unique_transform_stanza_name>] DEST_KEY not_equals _raw
check:           props.conf [<source type>] SEDCMD-<class> absent
check:           field_filters.conf [<fieldFilterName>] action absent
check:           indexes.conf [<index>] enableDataIntegrityControl in 1|true

external:        Confirming that a reduced view matches the stored record is a comparison
                 the assessor performs against the rawdata journal; the application
                 supplies the hashes that comparison uses.
external:        Protecting the index files from modification outside Splunk rests on
                 operating system file permissions and on the storage platform.

citation:        transforms.conf.spec:68 [<unique_transform_stanza_name>], :241 DEST_KEY =
                 <KEY> with the KEY list at the end of the file (_raw among them) and :244
                 "This setting is only valid for index-time field extractions";
                 props.conf.spec:1043 TRANSFORMS-<class>, :1243 SEDCMD-<class>;
                 field_filters.conf.spec:32, :37-70; indexes.conf.spec:594
                 enableDataIntegrityControl = <boolean> default false. The checks inventory
                 lists _raw against transforms.conf as undeclared because it is a DEST_KEY
                 value drawn from the specification's KEYS list rather than a setting name.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: a transform writing to DEST_KEY =
                 _raw, a SEDCMD class, or a field filter is applied to audit data, or
                 rawdata integrity hashing is not enabled on the audit indexes, so the
                 application's audit reduction does not demonstrably preserve the original
                 content of the records.
